only." 13194139534681 true] [17592186303137 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303138 13194139534681 true] [17592186303137 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303139 13194139534681 true] [17592186303137 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303140 13194139534681 true] [17592186303137 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303141 13194139534681 true] [17592186303137 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303142 13194139534681 true] [17592186303137 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534681 true] [17592186303137 1041 "selection" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303137 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303142 13194139534681 true] [17592186303137 1110 #uuid "d2a4d10c-c21d-558f-b943-31033714e15e" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303138 1034 "$(0,1)$ and $(2,3)$" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303138 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534681 true] [17592186303138 1111 #uuid "eec5bffe-f37b-542a-b883-24981acf56b0" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303139 1034 "$(0,1)$ only" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303139 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534681 true] [17592186303139 1111 #uuid "830cf24c-0dfa-5396-817d-7d783a1a481a" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303140 1034 "$(0,1)$ and $(1,2)$" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303140 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534681 true] [17592186303140 1111 #uuid "7495b2c2-665b-517b-a60b-9c61ed3ea1be" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303141 1034 "$(2,3)$ only" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303141 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534681 true] [17592186303141 1111 #uuid "c14260ea-f10e-52ce-bcc9-bed40a408717" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303142 1034 "$(1,2)$ only" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303142 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534681 true] [17592186303142 1111 #uuid "426ba1bd-081f-552d-a1fe-5c1a630db5c3" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303143 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303144 13194139534681 true] [17592186303143 1089 "q-114273" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303143 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534681 true] [17592186303143 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{2}(5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x),$ defined on $x\\in (0,\\infty ).$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)$ is concave up on $(0,e)$\n- $f(x)$ is concave down on $(0,e)$\n- $f(x)$ is concave down on $(e,\\infty )$" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303143 1113 #uuid "190520f8-9dd8-5a57-996e-9e323ff2fbe7" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303143 1145 "First, we calculate the second derivative of $f(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =2x(5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{x} \\\\  & =2x(5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-2x \\\\  & =2x(4-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =2(4-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-2x\\cdot \\frac{2}{x} \\\\  & =8-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-4 \\\\  & =4(1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the function is concave up, we need to solve ${f}^{″}(x)>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) & >0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡x & <1 \\\\ x & <e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ is concave up on  $(0,e).$\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is concave down when ${f}^{″}(x)<0.$ By similar reasoning to before, this leads to the inequality $4(1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)<0,$ which has the solution $(e,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303144 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303145 13194139534681 true] [17592186303144 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303146 13194139534681 true] [17592186303144 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303147 13194139534681 true] [17592186303144 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303148 13194139534681 true] [17592186303144 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303149 13194139534681 true] [17592186303144 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534681 true] [17592186303144 1041 "selection" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303144 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303146 13194139534681 true] [17592186303144 1110 #uuid "81dd3269-5b25-5a0a-b569-8ad866dc06e6" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303145 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303145 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534681 true] [17592186303145 1111 #uuid "2a8541dc-ddb3-5ff0-93eb-1a08c0d63907" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303146 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303146 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534681 true] [17592186303146 1111 #uuid "b3fc6cc2-0d44-55c0-a67b-40a19e3e8268" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303147 1034 "I only" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303147 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534681 true] [17592186303147 1111 #uuid "288f30aa-b0f9-57e9-a1b4-394b0093e7de" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303148 1034 "III only" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303148 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534681 true] [17592186303148 1111 #uuid "8187c10e-60f5-50a0-aef4-77358c06f650" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303149 1034 "II only" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303149 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534681 true] [17592186303149 1111 #uuid "a1b1be4f-07e2-5ad8-8ca9-60397cec6e75" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303150 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303151 13194139534681 true] [17592186303150 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303153 13194139534681 true] [17592186303150 1089 "q-344765" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303150 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534681 true] [17592186303150 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039567/assets/56265e4a47a878233f27b1e265158dc766aa410144dfe95a20ce7f672b797802.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\nThe graph of the second derivative $y={f}^{″}(x)$ of the function $f(x)$ intersects the $x$-axis at the points $x=-4$ and $x=1,$ as shown above. Find the interval on which the function $f(x)$ is concave up.\n\n$f(x)$ is concave up on the interval\n$(${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$).$" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303150 1113 #uuid "8b73c45f-5f0d-5b2f-a471-18a4d14cf315" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303150 1145 "A function $f(x)$ is concave up over an interval $(a,b)$ if ${f}^{″}(x)>0$ for all $x\\in (a,b).$\n\nFrom the plotted graph of $y={f}^{″}(x),$ we can see that ${f}^{″}(x)>0$ on the interval $(-4,1).$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is concave up on the interval $(\\,-4,1\\,).$" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303151 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303152 13194139534681 true] [17592186303151 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534681 true] [17592186303151 1041 "field-1" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303151 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303152 13194139534681 true] [17592186303151 1110 #uuid "47b9b341-fd9d-5477-82ec-50a7afee04aa" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303152 1034 "-4" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303152 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534681 true] [17592186303152 1111 #uuid "56dee1ba-5db2-59fe-98cd-630a61f37239" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303153 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303154 13194139534681 true] [17592186303153 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534681 true] [17592186303153 1041 "field-2" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303153 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303154 13194139534681 true] [17592186303153 1110 #uuid "013ea9f9-f4e6-575f-879c-8e6613dd51f6" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303154 1034 "1" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303154 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534681 true] [17592186303154 1111 #uuid "2e24f9b0-96c2-5d87-b824-91db1840ed10" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303155 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303156 13194139534681 true] [17592186303155 1089 "q-79047" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303155 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534681 true] [17592186303155 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)=2+3x-{e}^{-x}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)$ is concave down on $(-\\infty ,\\infty )$\n- $f(x)$ is concave up on $(0,\\infty )$\n- $f(x)$ is concave up on $(-\\infty ,0)$" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303155 1113 #uuid "61c5d722-ecbd-5ec6-af6e-19c6056c6975" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303155 1145 "First, we calculate the second derivative of $f(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =3+{e}^{-x} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-{e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${e}^{-x}>0$ for every real value of $x,$ it follows that $-{e}^{-x}<0$ for every real value of $x.$ Therefore, ${f}^{″}(x)$ is never positive, so there are no intervals where $f(x)$ is concave up.\n\nSince ${f}^{″}(x)<0$ for every real value of $x,$ the function is concave down on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303156 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303157 13194139534681 true] [17592186303156 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303158 13194139534681 true] [17592186303156 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303159 13194139534681 true] [17592186303156 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303160 13194139534681 true] [17592186303156 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303161 13194139534681 true] [17592186303156 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534681 true] [17592186303156 1041 "selection" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303156 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303158 13194139534681 true] [17592186303156 1110 #uuid "23372881-aa72-55f4-a6aa-aa4456e28bb5" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303157 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303157 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534681 true] [17592186303157 1111 #uuid "9bdb5fbc-d8d8-508b-a81b-e58c4e5c3185" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303158 1034 "I only" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303158 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534681 true] [17592186303158 1111 #uuid "3190e8ef-1a91-5d56-8172-676959ecf5ad" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303159 1034 "III only" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303159 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534681 true] [17592186303159 1111 #uuid "a597ab46-b4fe-56c0-8bd8-a22088dd5474" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303160 1034 "None of the statements are true." 13194139534681 true] [17592186303160 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534681 true] [17592186303160 1111 #uuid "1b6b87ca-5c95-5b6e-ac81-adb346366952" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303161 1034 "II only" 13194139534681 true] [17592186303161 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534681 true] [17592186303161 1111 #uuid "00c522ea-b536-579c-96e8-6988188dc464" 13194139534681 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-114060" 17592186303129 "q-114060/selection" 17592186303130 "q-114060/selection/47130c0